From: pocknix <pocknix@arcadematicas>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add a ~95C passive trip + GPU devfreq cooling map

The gpuss0..7 thermal zones ship only hot (120 C) and critical (125 C) trips
with no cooling map, so a full-speed Adreno 830 can run away towards a thermal
shutdown (~101 C at the top OPPs). Add a passive trip at 95 C on each gpuss
zone mapped to the GPU devfreq cooling device (devfreq-3d00000.gpu), so the GPU
is throttled before the critical trip is ever reached.

Reported by WhiteEagle-12 (Holodor) in arcadematicas/pocknix-odin3-support#1.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi	2026-10-09 20:44:06.949193521 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi	2026-10-09 20:44:06.963521693 +0200
@@ -7284,6 +7284,12 @@
 			thermal-sensors = <&tsens2 1>;
 
 			trips {
+				gpuss0_alert: gpuss0-alert {
+					temperature = <95000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
 				trip-point0 {
 					temperature = <120000>;
 					hysteresis = <5000>;
@@ -7295,6 +7301,13 @@
 					hysteresis = <0>;
 					type = "critical";
 				};
+
+			cooling-maps {
+				gpuss0_cdev: gpuss0-cdev {
+					trip = <&gpuss0_alert>;
+					cooling-device = <&gpu THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+				};
+			};
 			};
 		};
 
